# Cyclotomic `W₁₂`/`W₂₄` Operator Galois Groups (`V₄ ≅ C₂ × C₂` and `C₂ × C₂ × C₂`), Nilpotency Bounds, `n`-Potent Symmetry Sandwiches, Bipartite Drazin–Moore–Penrose Attention, and Sylvester Operator Matrices

This module formalizes the 8-stage acyclic causal poset
`CNS₀ ≺ CNS₁ ≺ CNS₂ ≺ CNS₃ ≺ CNS₄ ≺ CNS₅ ≺ CNS₆ ≺ CNS₇` extracted by epistemic compilation
(`solve et coagula`) from Turns 166–217 of `1ofaG3fBD1VlprR7ShtsdctpOVRjmjB9f` and the
non-commutative operator-ring theory of `W₁₂`/`W₂₄` cyclotomic Galois groups, nilpotency exponent bounds,
`n`-potents, invertible symmetry sandwiches `G (·) G⁻¹`, and Sylvester operator matrices.

All theorems are proved universally over arbitrary non-commutative associative operator rings
`[Ring B]` (and `[StarRing B]` where involutions appear), with concrete non-commutative matrix
witnesses in `Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) ℤ` and `Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) ℤ` certifying
non-commutativity (`T16`) and non-vacuity (`T17`).

## Main Definitions and Theorems

1. **Stage `CNS₀` (`drazin_mp_universal_sandwich_collapse` and
   `dmp_residual_qgt_and_anamnesis_tetraktys_closure`)**:
   - Universal Drazin–Moore–Penrose sandwich collapse `P * Mdag * P = (B_inv * M * Mdag) * M * (Mdag * M * B_inv) = B_inv`
     and zero-mode cone annihilation `conePlus P Mdag * M = 0`, `M * coneMinus P Mdag = 0`,
     `qgtMinus P Mdag Mdag * M = 0`, `M * qgtMinus P Mdag Mdag = 0`.
   - Orthogonal forward split `dmpOp P Mdag * mpdOp P Mdag = peirce11 P Mdag * peirce11 P Mdag + qgtPlus P Mdag Mdag`,
     QKV transfer duality `qgtPlus P Mdag Mdag * conePlus P Mdag = conePlus P Mdag * qgtMinus P Mdag Mdag = genV P Mdag Mdag * conePlus P Mdag`,
     and Anamnesis commutator closure `[P, T_DMP] = +N_+`, `[P, T_MPD] = -N_-` generating `(Φ, J, V, Σ)`.
2. **Stage `CNS₁` (`recursive_peirce_jordan_wigner_fermionization`,
   `tensor_train_peirce_decomposition`, `rope_tetraktys_and_tcr_former_causal_unrolling`,
   and `recursive_daughter_chart_idempotence_and_parent_actions`)**:
   - Jordan–Wigner chiral string `invS P0` twisting commuting orthogonal-site raising operators
     into anticommuting fermionic operators `anticomm sig0 (invS P0 * sig1) = 0`.
   - 3-site orthogonal Peirce Tensor-Train reconstruction `ttReconstruct3 P1 P2 P3 M = M`,
     square-zero inter-site entanglement bonds `ttBond P_k P_j M`, and nearest-neighbor MPS
     truncation residual `M - mpsApprox3 P1 P2 P3 M = ttBond P1 P3 M + ttBond P3 P1 M`.
   - RoPE vs. TCR-Former causal truncation (`conePlus P A = 0`) and recursive confinement of the
     daughter Tetraktys `(V₁, Σ₁, Φ₁, J₁)` generated by `P₁ = idemTrans P A` inside `P`.
3. **Stage `CNS₂` (`fubini_study_bkm_star_gramian_and_unipotent_exponential_coordinates`)**:
   - Over `[Ring B] [StarRing B]` with `P * P = P`, `star P = P`, and `star X = X`, proves
     `star (conePlus P X) = coneMinus P X`, `genV P X X = conePlus P X * star (conePlus P X) + star (conePlus P X) * conePlus P X`,
     and emergent unipotent exponential coordinates `expConePlus P A t = 1 + t • conePlus P A`
     generating `(t * s) • genV P A C` and `(t * s) • genSig P A C`.
4. **Stage `CNS₃` (`nilpotent_first_peirce_sl2_reconstruction` and
   `nilpotency_exponent_bound_ladder_and_unipotent_inverse`)**:
   - Nilpotent-first reconstruction of orthogonal idempotents `P_em = N_+ * N_-`, `Q_em = N_- * N_+`
     and the Cartan `𝔰𝔩₂`-triple `H_em = comm N_+ N_- = P_em - Q_em` (`comm H_em N_+ = 2 • N_+`,
     `comm H_em N_- = -(2 • N_-)`) from a von Neumann regular pair of order-2 nilpotents.
   - Nilpotency exponent bounds (`IsNilpotentOfIndexAtMost N n`) and universal geometric series
     inverse `(1 - N) * (∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, N ^ k) = 1 - N ^ n`.
5. **Stage `CNS₄` (`symmetry_sandwich_preserves_powers_npotents_and_nilpotency_bounds`)**:
   - Invertible symmetry sandwich `symmetrySandwich G G_inv X = G * X * G_inv` (`G * G_inv = 1`,
     `G_inv * G = 1`) is a strict ring automorphism satisfying
     `(symmetrySandwich G G_inv X) ^ n = symmetrySandwich G G_inv (X ^ n)` for all `n : ℕ`,
     preserving idempotents, `n`-potents (`IsNPotent X n`), nilpotency exponent bounds
     (`IsNilpotentOfIndexAtMost N n`), exact nilpotency indices, and all Peirce Tetraktys
     generators `(Φ, J, V, Σ)`.
6. **Stage `CNS₅` (`w12_w24_galois_groups_klein_v4_and_c2_cube` and
   `w12_w24_cyclotomic_operator_galois_conjugates_and_symmetry_invariance`)**:
   - `W₁₂` (`opPhi12 X = X ^ 4 - X ^ 2 + 1`) has Galois group `(ZMod 12)ˣ = {1, 5, 7, 11} ≅ C₂ × C₂ = V₄`
     (Klein four-group, `∀ u : (ZMod 12)ˣ, u ^ 2 = 1`), and `W₂₄` (`opPhi24 X = X ^ 8 - X ^ 4 + 1`)
     has Galois group `(ZMod 24)ˣ = {1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23} ≅ C₂ × C₂ × C₂`
     (elementary abelian 2-group of order 8, `∀ u : (ZMod 24)ˣ, u ^ 2 = 1`).
   - Over any non-commutative `[Ring B]`, if `opPhi12 X = 0` (resp. `opPhi24 X = 0`), then all 4
     `V₄` Galois power conjugates `X ^ k` (`k ∈ {1, 5, 7, 11}`) (resp. all 8 `C₂ × C₂ × C₂` Galois
     power conjugates `X ^ k`, `k ∈ {1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23}`) and all their invertible
     symmetry sandwiches `symmetrySandwich G G_inv (X ^ k)` are exact roots of `opPhi12` (resp. `opPhi24`)!
7. **Stage `CNS₆` (`operator_polynomials_over_idempotents_tripotents_and_nilpotents`)**:
   - Polynomial collapse over idempotents (`P ^ (k + 1) = P`), Sylvester–Lagrange spectral
     projectors `(T ^ 2 + T, T ^ 2 - T, 1 - T ^ 2)` of a tripotent `T ^ 3 = T`, and their
     covariance under `symmetrySandwich G G_inv`.
8. **Stage `CNS₇` (`sylvester_operator_matrix_unipotent_diagonalization_and_powers`)**:
   - Non-commutative Sylvester block operator matrices `sylvesterBlockMat A C Y = !![A, Y; 0, C]`
     in `Matrix (Fin 2) (Fin 2) B`, unipotent nilpotent-sandwich transformation
     `sylvesterUnipotentG (-X) * sylvesterBlockMat A C Y * sylvesterUnipotentG X = sylvesterBlockMat A C (Y + (A * X - X * C))`,
     all-power intertwining `sylvesterBlockMat A C (X * C - A * X) ^ k = sylvesterBlockMat (A ^ k) (C ^ k) (X * C ^ k - A ^ k * X)`,
     and exact evaluation of `opPhi12` and `opPhi24` on Sylvester operator matrices!
